From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 03:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 102/104] Let a platform set the default keyboard backlight
 idle timeout

`idle.keyboardBacklight` is opt-in per user in shell.json, which the shell never deep-merges, so neither a fresh install nor an existing one can get a machine's default from the package that knows the machine. A platform package can now name one as data in the platform root, `/usr/share/omarchy-platform/idle.json` (`{"keyboardBacklight": <seconds>}`), read the way `audio.json` is. A shell.json value wins, 0 included; without either the timeout stays off.

The timeout runs only where a `*kbd_backlight*` LED exists, so a platform default reaches a machine without one as a no-op. When the timeout comes on (at session start, once the LED is found) the service runs `restore`, which brings back a level a blank left dark across a reboot and does nothing otherwise.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
